WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.392
You move a task to Done.

00:00:02.392 --> 00:00:04.505
An older save overwrites it.

00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:05.666
And back it goes.

00:00:05.666 --> 00:00:08.475
Technically saved. Practically gone.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.471
Claudex Loop is an open-source workflow

00:00:11.471 --> 00:00:14.164
connecting Claude Code and Codex.

00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:15.766
One prepares the plan.

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:19.600
The other challenges it.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.600
Could an older save erase a newer edit?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.315
Revise the plan: reject outdated saves.

00:00:28.315 --> 00:00:30.400
And test both edits.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.900
First, reproduce the failure.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.900
Then build the version check.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.942
Replay it. The old save is rejected.

00:00:41.942 --> 00:00:46.100
Your edit survives.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.234
The other provider inspects the finished code.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:53.000
Agreement isn't proof. Test the behavior.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.322
Comment REVIEW for the setup guide

00:00:55.322 --> 00:00:59.000
and example test on our site.
